messages:
Aisha: Heads-up  CorporateBank wants a short hands-on demo for their SREs + security team. Key asks: live streaming SDK example with function/tool calling, schema-validated structured output, and a one-page pricing delta between hosted streaming and a Dedicated 2G commit. Can we assemble?

Leo: I can do the SDK examples. Quick clarifying q: do they want websockets-style streaming (sdk stream callback) or server-sent events? They said low-latency edits so websockets is preferable.

Aisha: Websockets/SDK stream. Also must show a pattern for functions that fetch internal customer metadata (auth via service account) and how we surface missing fields gracefully.

Dani: I'll draft the short security FAQ answers: data tenancy, key management, logs redaction, SOC2/ISO attestation, sub-processors. I need their Qs; can you paste the doc?

Aisha: Pasted top-6 security Qs into the drive link: (1) Are tokens logged? (2) Can we bring our KMS? (3) Do you support VPC-only control plane? (4) Retention & deletions? (5) List of subprocessors. (6) Is function-call metadata stored?

Leo: For the sample code (Node):

```js
// simplified websocket-style streaming with function call
const client = new RedwoodWSClient(process.env.REDWOOD_WS_URL, apiKey);
client.on('token', t => process.stdout.write(t));
client.on('function_call', async fc => {
  if (fc.name === 'get_customer_meta') {
    const res = await fetch(`https://internal-api/customers/${fc.args.id}`, { headers: { 'Authorization': 'Bearer ' + SA_TOKEN }});
    const json = await res.json();
    client.sendFunctionResult(fc.id, JSON.stringify(json));
  }
});
client.send({ model: 'redwood-1-stream', stream: true, function_call: 'auto', schema: {type: 'object', properties: {intent:{type:'string'},payload:{type:'object'}}, required:['intent']}});
```

Leo: Note: include a short snippet showing fallback when function fails (return minimal text answer + structured error object).

Dani: Security answers draft: tokens are not stored by default in production hosted; short-term request logs may contain obfuscated token metadata for debugging, PII is redacted by default with configurable redaction rules. We support customer-managed KMS (bring-your-own) and HSM via our Private deployment. VPC-only control plane available for enterprise Private. Retention configurable up to 36 months; immediate deletion via API for committed enterprise configs. Subprocessors list is in the legal portal, I'll pull the latest. Function-call metadata: by default calls are logged with minimal metadata; bodies can be opted-out of logging.

Sam: I'll sketch the pricing delta table. Quick notes: hosted streaming unit price (input+output token) for discussion; Dedicated 2G commit: flat monthly price, expected sustained tokens/sec ~ 12k depending on model and sequence length, and cost-per-token drops ~ 40-60% vs hosted at high volume. I'll produce example math for 1M, 10M, 100M tokens and a 3-month vs 12-month commit comparison.

Aisha: Also include a short runbook for SEs to debug streaming issues onsite: check websocket handshake (401), inspect keepalive intervals, capture partial JSON fragments and show a JSON-repair helper, and how to toggle streaming chunk size in the SDK.

infra-bot: Demo environment ready: env=corpbank-presales-1780123456, endpoint=https://demo.redwood.example/corpbank-presales-1780123456, creds=shared-vault:corpbank-presales

Leo: For structured output validation we should show ajv-based validation and a small example schema: {"type":"object","properties":{"intent":{"type":"string"},"customer_id":{"type":"string"},"actions":{"type":"array"}},"required":["intent","customer_id"]} and show a small server snippet rejecting invalid messages with a clear error object.

Dani: Add a canned line for the security doc: "We can sign a targeted DPA and support specific jurisdictional data residency controls via Private deployment or Hosted with region locks." I'll mark anything requiring legal review.

Sam: I'll add an appendix to the pricing one-pager with sensitivity analysis: if sequences average 2k tokens vs 5k tokens, throughput & cost change significantly. Also plan a quick throughput demo script: 10 concurrent editors for 2 minutes, record average latency and tokens/sec.

Aisha: Action items before EOD: Leo -> repo with 2 SDK examples (websocket streaming + REST fallback) + small README; Sam -> pricing table + delta math; Dani -> security FAQ draft + pointers for legal; I'll assemble into a one-pager and drop into the SFDC attachment. Review 8:30am PT tomorrow.

Leo: Will do. I'll also include a tiny troubleshooting CLI to repair truncated JSON from partial streams.

Dani: Legal flagged subprocessors list update; looping in legal after I finish answers.

Sam: POC runbook note: suggest starting on Hosted with a small traffic generator, then switch routing to Dedicated pool via routing tag for step-up testing. Include rollback steps to Hosted.

Aisha: Thanks all ":raised_hands:". If anything needs an expedited legal or pricing approval ping me directly.
